st line.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    bg = max(set(x for row in grid for x in row),\n             key=lambda x: sum(row.count(x) for row in grid))\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Each adjacent, same-colored diagonal pair defines a line to extend\n    # outward in both directions, stopping at existing non-background cells.\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            color = grid[r][c]\n            if color == bg:\n                continue\n            for dc in (-1, 1):\n                r2, c2 = r + 1, c + dc\n                if not (0 <= r2 < h and 0 <= c2 < w) or grid[r2][c2] != color:\n                    continue\n\n                for rr, cc, dr, dcol in (\n                    (r, c, -1, -dc),\n                    (r2, c2, 1, dc),\n                ):\n                    rr += dr\n                    cc += dcol\n                    while 0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w and grid[rr][cc] == bg:\n                        out[rr][cc] = color\n                        rr += dr\n                        cc += dcol\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":62,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1792666102.546,"t1":1792666150.696,"alias":"task-cd2782a0","message":"Your program was checked on demo pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 5\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 5 6\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 5 6 6\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 5 6 6 6\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 5 6 6 6 6\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 5 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 5 6 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 5 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 6 6 6 6 5 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 6 6 6 5 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 6 6 5 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 6 5 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 5 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n9 5 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n5 1 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 1 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 6 1 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n6 6 6 6 1 6 